      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In my experience amount of avatars, experience, and veteran status have no bearing on whether people optimize or not. It's all about the person, and while veterans are probably more likely to be optimizers, there's no guarantee of it and plenty of veterans got their status by making crazy avatars that really do lag on most machines regardless of optimization.\n\nWhat they really need is a system that affects optimization at all levels to replace their poly count system.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-26T22:31:21.573Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "They remove of the veteran rank in my mind was actually a bad decision. I had my safety features setup so only that rank had particles enabled. If someone has been able to achieve that rank more often then not everything they have will be optimized well. Please do not remove it because people want to turn it into a popularity contest. It serves a purpose. If you have to change the name to creator or something similar to stop the popularly contest do that.",
